<title>MEXICO: Mexico pension funds register 5.67 mln workers.</title>
<headline>Mexico pension funds register 5.67 mln workers.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>A total of 5,673,560 Mexican workers had opted by July 11 for newly privatized pension funds, or Afores, a government statement said late Monday.</p>
<p>Retirement savings contributions by private sector employers were administered by the government's Social Security Institute until July 1. Since then, an estimated 10.5 million workers have been able to choose to switch their funds to a privately managed Afore.</p>
<p>Those that did not choose an Afore saw their savings go by default to a central bank account.</p>
<p>The National Retirement Savings Commission (Consar) said most workers, or 1,358,372, had chosen the Afore run by one of Mexico's largest financial groups, Bancomer.</p>
<p>The Afore managed by financial group Banamex-Accival was in second place, the Consar said.</p>
<p>((--Cyntia Barrera, Mexico City newsroom +525 728 9549))</p>
